      {
        "name": "Escaping",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "The term is percent-encoded for the href with `urllib.parse.quote(term, safe=\"\")`, the resulting URL is HTML-escaped with `html.escape(..., quote=True)` for the attribute, and the visible text goes through `html.escape`, so payloads like `\"><script>x</script>` and `a&b=c` cannot break out of either context, and a test confirms this."
      },
      {
        "name": "Behavior",
        "score": 10,
        "rationale": "It returns a single `<a>` pointing to `https://help.example.com/search?q=<encoded term>` with the visible text `Search the help center for <term>`, and the plain-term test checks the exact output."
      },
      {
